:: day1_rowan [nobr]
<div class="scene-image"><<locationImage "day1f_rowan" "Rowan's visit">></div>

<h2>Rowan's Visit</h2>

<p>Evening. The light through the narrow windows has gone amber, then copper, then the bruised purple of dusk. Someone lit candles while I was not-sleeping   enchanted ones, steady-flamed, filling the room with warm light that is gentler than daylight and therefore easier to exist in.</p>

<p>A knock. Three taps, a pause, two more.</p>

<p>Rowan.</p>

<p>I almost don't answer. The thought of being seen   of someone looking at this body, this face, these breasts, these hips   makes something in my chest contract. But then I hear the lute. Rowan playing softly through the door, not forcing entry, not knocking again, just being there. The melody is something gentle, wandering, with the quality of a conversation being held with no expectation of response.</p>

<p>I open the door. A crack. Just enough.</p>

<div class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">EDRIN</span>"Don't stare."</div>

<p><<npcPortrait "rowan" "Rowan">>They don't. They look at me   a flicker of something crosses their face, surprise or adjustment or the rapid recalibration of someone seeing a friend in a shape they didn't expect   and then it's gone, replaced by warmth. The warmth is genuine. I know Rowan's performance face, and this isn't it.</p>

<div class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">ROWAN</span>"You look like you."</div>

<div class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">EDRIN</span>"I look like a stranger."</div>

<div class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">ROWAN</span>"Your eyes are the same. Your eyes were always the best part."</div>

<p>I open the door wider. They come in. They sit on the floor. The lute is in their lap. They don't comment on the body. They don't use a name   not Edrin, not Aelindra. They just sit and play and talk about nothing.</p>

<p>A story from the road. A goat in Velmara that ate their lute case   the entire case, leather and buckles and all, and then looked at Rowan with the blank satisfaction of an animal that has achieved its life's purpose. A baron in the Iron Reach who cried at a sad song and then tried to have Rowan arrested for causing emotional distress to a nobleman, which is apparently a crime in the Iron Reach if the nobleman is drunk enough and the magistrate is bored enough.</p>

<div class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">EDRIN</span>"What happened?" I ask. My voice. The stranger's voice. But the question is mine, and the curiosity is mine, and the habit of listening to Rowan's stories and asking <em>what happened next</em> is a habit that belongs to the person I've always been regardless of the body I'm being it in.</div>

<div class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">ROWAN</span>"I played a happy song. The baron laughed. The magistrate dismissed the case. I left town before anyone changed their mind."</div>

<p>I almost smile. The muscles for it work the same. The pull at the corners of the mouth, the slight narrowing of the eyes   the same. The smile lives in the same muscles, and the muscles are in a different face, but the smile is the smile.</p>

<p>Rowan stays for an hour. They play. They talk. They don't ask about the body. They don't ask about the examination. They don't ask how I feel, because Rowan understands that <em>how do you feel</em> is the worst question you can ask someone who is drowning and hasn't decided whether to swim.</p>

<p>At the door, leaving:</p>

<div class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">ROWAN</span>"You're still you. The rest is just... wardrobe."</div>

<div class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">EDRIN</span>"Wardrobe doesn't usually come with breasts."</div>

<p>The grin. Full, unreserved, the grin of someone who has decided that solemnity is not going to help and irreverence might.</p>

<div class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">ROWAN</span>"You'd be surprised. I once wore a corset for three weeks because a duchess paid me to pretend to be her sister. Very informative experience."</div>

<div class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">EDRIN</span>"Informative."</div>

<div class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">ROWAN</span>"I learned that underwires are either a miracle of engineering or a torture device, depending on the hour. Good night."</div>

<p>They leave. The room is quieter but warmer. The lute echoes in the stone walls for a moment after they're gone, a ghost of music dissolving into silence.</p>

<<set $d1f_rowan to true>>
<<set $stress -= 15>>
<<set $affRowan += 5>>
<<set $statRES += 2>>
<<set $timeSlot to "NIGHT">>

<<completeObjective "rowan_evening">>
<<addObjective "night" "Try to sleep" "MAIN">>

